<Concept title="Equip Legality (class × weapon type)" section="Mechanics">
  <p>The key words <strong>MUST</strong> / <strong>MUST NOT</strong> / <strong>SHOULD</strong> are used as in RFC 2119. This page defines <strong>which classes can equip which weapon types</strong> — the normative contract behind the Equip menu, the field-HUD weapon picker, storage, and the weapon shop.</p>

  <h2>Contract</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Single source of truth:</strong> a weapon's equippability for a class is determined by <code>ClassData.allowed_weapon_types</code> (a list of <code>WeaponType</code> ids). It is the <em>only</em> input — <code>WeaponData.usable_by</code> MUST NOT be consulted for legality (it has drifted from the class lists; see Issues).</li>
    <li><strong>One shared predicate:</strong> every screen that asks "can this be equipped?" MUST route through a single helper, returning <code>&#123; ok, reason, slot &#125;</code>. No per-screen class checks (the Alpha pattern this replaces had four divergent copies).</li>
    <li><strong>Level gate:</strong> equipping a weapon also requires <code>character.level &ge; weapon.level</code>. A failure here yields a distinct reason ("Requires Lv N").</li>
    <li><strong>Reasons are surfaced:</strong> when a weapon can't be equipped, the UI MUST show <em>why</em> (greyed Equip option + reason), never a silent omission.</li>
    <li><strong>Debug bypass:</strong> <code>DebugConfig.equip_all</code> (System menu / <code>PSZ_DEBUG_WEAPONS</code>) bypasses the class + level gates so any weapon can be equipped to verify its model — it MUST affect only the legality gate, nothing else.</li>
  </ul>

